  "solution": {
    "text": "Given $f(x)=\\tan ^{-1}\\left(\\frac{2 x}{1-x^2}\\right)$ for $x \\in(-1,1)$\nclearly range of $f(x)=\\left(-\\frac{\\pi}{2}, \\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right)$.\n$\\therefore$ co-domain of function $=B=\\left(-\\frac{\\pi}{2}, \\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right)$.",
